# enq_known: A1 moves from "has no need to enquire" to "cannot enquire". In A1, "can" leans toward "has a point in enquiring". In C, it reads as possibility, matching the unknown case. The text attributes "cannot" to both cases jointly, so I read it as one sense. The weak point is the bridge A1 itself, not a shift in the claim.
# knows_subject / enq_unknown: the familiar reply is that "not know" equivocates between total ignorance and partial knowledge. But every statement here uses "does not know" the same way, so I did not mark it.
